### Bonus drills

```bash
grep -c "WARN" app.log                 # count of warnings (expected: 3)
grep -A 1 "ERROR" app.log              # each error plus the line after it
grep "ERROR" app.log | sort | uniq     # combine grep with sort and uniq
grep -r "ERROR" .                      # search every file in the current folder
```

## grep flags I learned

| Flag | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `-i` | ignore case |
| `-n` | show line numbers |
| `-v` | invert (lines that do NOT match) |
| `-c` | count matching lines |
| `-r` | search recursively through folders |
| `-A N` | show N lines after each match |

## Other tools from the freeCodeCamp section

- `sort`: orders lines alphabetically or numerically
- `uniq`: removes adjacent duplicates (run `sort` first)
- `find`: locates files, e.g. `find . -name "*.conf"`
- `diff`: compares two files line by line

